            <ArticleTitle>Costal exostoses as an unusual cause of spontaneous hemothorax.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>135</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1186/s13019-015-0342-6</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 20-year-old male presented with chest pain lasting several days. A radiologic examination revealed pleural effusion in the right hemithorax. Video-assisted thoracoscopic surgery demonstrated a bleeding focus at the diaphragm caused by injury due to a costal exostosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
